  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(n)$ be the minimal integer $m$ such that $n$ is the sum of the $k$ smallest divisors of $m$ for some $k\\geq 1$.\nIs it true that $f(n)=o(n)$? Or is this true only for almost all $n$, and $\\limsup f(n)/n=\\infty$?",
